colemak caws is built around colemak to combine the most popular mods: [curl](https://colemakmods.github.io/ergonomic-mods/curl.html), [angle](https://colemakmods.github.io/ergonomic-mods/angle.html), [wide](https://colemakmods.github.io/ergonomic-mods/wide.html), [symbols](https://colemakmods.github.io/ergonomic-mods/symbols.html), (recommend clicking through those links - lots of pretty pictures and well-written explanations of *what all this is for*)

most of the work on it was done by [DreymaR](https://dreymar.colemak.org/)
this version is a phonetically equivalent cyrillic adaptation

# # main idea

the russian layout is built as a phonetic counterpart to the english one:

- A == А
- R == Р
- S == С
- T == Т
- G == Г

and so on, as far as possible

this approach lets you skip learning a new layout for cyrillic and type pretty confidently right away, knowing just the main layout.

# ? why this works for russian

letter and sound frequencies in russian and english are pretty similar in many ways, so phonetically mapping the english layout onto russian gives a decent distribution of load without deep optimization for russian texts.

([some wikipedia stuff about russian](https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A7%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%82%D0%BD%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C), [some wikipedia stuff about english](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Letter_frequency) )


